.Dd June 5, 2026
.Dt SERVICED 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm serviced
.Nd 5BSD capability-based service manager
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl d Ar manifest_dir
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the service manager for 5BSD.
It is started by
.Xr oracled 8
as a single child process via
.Xr pdfork 2
and inherits a cap_rt pair channel for requesting capability tokens,
pairs, and coalitions from the oracle.
.Pp
.Nm
reads service manifests (UCL files) from a manifest directory,
topologically sorts them by dependency, and launches each service via
.Xr pdfork 2 .
It supervises service lifecycle through
.Xr kqueue 2
process descriptors, enforces restart policies with linear backoff
and circuit-breaker protection, and operates a naming registry that
allows services to discover and connect to each other by
reverse-domain names.
.Pp
Administrative commands are sent via
.Xr servicectl 8
over a local control socket.
.Ss Startup Sequence
.Nm
executes the following phases during startup:
.Bl -enum
.It
Inherit the pair fd from the
.Ev ORACLED_PAIR_FD
environment variable and optional delegated service instance fds from
.Ev SERVICED_PAIR_SVC_FD ,
.Ev SERVICED_COALITION_SVC_FD ,
and
.Ev SERVICED_CAPPROTECT_FD .
.It
Apply a capprotect shield if a capprotect service instance fd was
inherited, hardening the process against ptrace, wait, scheduler
manipulation, and ktrace.
The shield does not block signals, allowing
.Dv SIGHUP
and
.Dv SIGTERM
from
.Xr oracled 8 .
The capprotect fd is closed after use.
.It
Create a
.Xr kqueue 2
and register the oracle pair fd for EOF detection (oracle death).
.It
Create a control socket at
.Pa /var/run/serviced.sock .
.It
Register signal handlers for
.Dv SIGTERM ,
.Dv SIGINT ,
.Dv SIGHUP ,
and
.Dv SIGCHLD .
.It
Send
.Dv ORACLE_OP_READY
to
.Xr oracled 8
on the pair channel.
.It
Load service manifests from the manifest directory, topologically sort
by dependency, and fork/exec each service via
.Xr pdfork 2 .
.It
Enter the event loop, monitoring services via process descriptors,
pair channels, coalition events, control socket connections, signals,
and restart timers.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "-d manifest_dir"
.It Fl d Ar manifest_dir
Read service manifests from
.Ar manifest_dir
instead of the directory specified by the
.Ev SERVICED_MANIFEST_DIR
environment variable or the default
.Pa /etc/serviced.d .
.El
.Sh INHERITED FILE DESCRIPTORS
.Nm
inherits the following file descriptors from
.Xr oracled 8 :
.Bl -tag -width "capprotect (fd 6)"
.It pair (fd 3)
Cap_rt pair channel back to
.Xr oracled 8 .
Used to request capability tokens, pairs, and coalitions.
Always required.
.It pair_svc (fd 4)
Delegated cap_rt pair service instance.
Allows
.Nm
to create pair channels for its children directly, without
round-tripping through
.Xr oracled 8 .
Optional.
.It coalition_svc (fd 5)
Delegated cap_rt coalition service instance.
Allows
.Nm
to create coalitions for process grouping.
Optional.
.It capprotect (fd 6)
Delegated capprotect service instance.
.Nm
uses this to apply an integrity shield at startup, then closes the fd.
Optional.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "SERVICED_COALITION_SVC_FD"
.It Ev ORACLED_PAIR_FD
File descriptor number for the cap_rt pair channel back to
.Xr oracled 8 .
Always 3.
Required.
.It Ev SERVICED_PAIR_SVC_FD
File descriptor number for the delegated pair service instance.
Optional.
.It Ev SERVICED_COALITION_SVC_FD
File descriptor number for the delegated coalition service instance.
Optional.
.It Ev SERVICED_CAPPROTECT_FD
File descriptor number for the delegated capprotect service instance.
Optional.
.It Ev SERVICED_MANIFEST_DIR
Directory containing service manifest files.
Overridden by the
.Fl d
flag.
Default:
.Pa /etc/serviced.d .
.It Ev SERVICED_CONTROL_SOCKET
Path for the control socket.
Default:
.Pa /var/run/serviced.sock .
Optional.
.El
.Sh SERVICE MANIFESTS
Service manifests are UCL files in the manifest directory.
Each
.Pa *.ucl
file declares one service.
Files are loaded in lexicographic order and topologically sorted
by dependency before launch.
Invalid manifests are logged and skipped.
.Pp
A maximum of 64 services may be loaded.
.Pp
The following keys are supported:
.Bl -tag -width "max_failures"
.It Va label Pq required
Unique name for the service.
Used in log messages, dependency references, the naming registry,
and control socket responses.
Maximum 63 characters.
.It Va program Pq required
Absolute path to the service binary.
Must be executable.
.It Va description
Human-readable description.
Cosmetic only.
.It Va user
Run the service as this user.
Sets uid, gid, and supplementary groups via
.Xr getpwnam 3
and
.Xr getgrouplist 3 .
Credential failures are fatal to prevent privilege escalation.
.It Va group
Run the service with this primary group.
Overrides the group from
.Va user
if both are set.
.It Va restart
Restart policy when the service exits.
One of:
.Dq never
(default),
.Dq always ,
or
.Dq on-failure
(restart only on non-zero exit).
.It Va stop_timeout
Seconds to wait after
.Dv SIGTERM
before sending
.Dv SIGKILL .
Clamped to the range 1\(en300.
Default: 5.
.It Va max_failures
Circuit breaker threshold.
After this many consecutive rapid failures, the service is permanently
disabled until the next manifest reload.
Clamped to the range 1\(en100.
Default: 10.
.It Va provides
Array of capability names this service provides.
Maximum 8 entries.
Used by the dependency graph to determine start order.
Names must be unique across all loaded manifests.
.It Va requires
Array of capability names this service depends on.
Maximum 8 entries.
The service will not start until all required capabilities are
available.
.It Va capabilities
Object containing capability tokens to delegate to the service.
See
.Sx Capabilities
below.
.It Va jail
Object describing a jail to create for the service.
See
.Sx Jail
below.
.El
.Ss Capabilities
The
.Va capabilities
object may contain the following arrays:
.Bl -tag -width "network"
.It Va paths
Array of absolute filesystem paths (maximum 16).
.Nm
requests an isolation access token for each path from the oracle
and passes it to the service.
.It Va files
Array of fine-grained file capability objects (maximum 16).
Each object has:
.Bl -tag -width "actions" -compact
.It Va path
Target file path (required).
.It Va actions
A string or array of
.Dv FI_FS_*
operation names:
.Dq read ,
.Dq write ,
.Dq exec ,
.Dq create ,
.Dq delete ,
.Dq stat ,
.Dq lookup ,
.Dq append ,
.Dq rename_from ,
.Dq rename_to ,
.Dq link ,
.Dq setattr ,
.Dq truncate ,
.Dq uipc_connect ,
or
.Dq *
/
.Dq all
for all operations.
.El
.It Va network
Array of network endpoint objects (maximum 16).
Each object has:
.Bl -tag -width "direction" -compact
.It Va domain
Address family:
.Dq inet
(default),
.Dq inet6 ,
or
.Dq * .
.It Va protocol
Transport protocol:
.Dq tcp ,
.Dq udp ,
or
.Dq * .
.It Va port
Integer port number, or
.Dq * .
.It Va ports
Port range as
.Dq min-max ,
or
.Dq * .
.It Va direction
.Dq bind
(default),
.Dq connect ,
or
.Dq * .
.It Va address
IP address or CIDR notation (optional).
.It Va prefix
CIDR prefix length (optional).
.El
.It Va jails
Array of jail operation tokens (maximum 16).
Grants the service authority to perform jail operations.
.It Va system
Array of system gate names (e.g.,
.Dq kldload ,
.Dq reboot ,
.Dq sysctl ) .
.Nm
requests a system access token from the oracle with the specified
gates.
.El
.Ss Jail
The optional
.Va jail
object creates a jail for the service at launch time:
.Bl -tag -width "hostname"
.It Va name Pq required
Jail name.
.It Va path Pq required
Root filesystem path for the jail.
.It Va hostname
Hostname inside the jail.
.It Va ip4
IPv4 address to assign to the jail.
.El
.Sh SERVICE ENVIRONMENT
Each launched service receives a minimal environment:
.Bl -tag -width "ORACLED_TOKEN_FDS"
.It Ev PATH
.Pa /sbin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin
.It Ev ORACLED_PAIR_FD
File descriptor number for the cap_rt pair channel back to
.Nm
(always 3).
Services use this via
.Xr libservice 3
to report readiness, register names, and look up other services.
.It Ev ORACLED_TOKEN_FDS
Comma-separated list of file descriptor numbers for capability
tokens (starting at 4).
Only set if the manifest declares capabilities.
.It Ev ORACLED_LABEL
The service label from the manifest.
.It Ev USER
Set if
.Va user
is specified in the manifest.
.It Ev HOME
Home directory of the service user.
Only set when
.Va user
is specified.
.El
.Pp
Standard I/O (fds 0, 1, 2) is redirected to
.Pa /dev/null .
All file descriptors above the token range are closed via
.Xr closefrom 2 .
.Sh SERVICE LIFECYCLE
.Ss Dependency Sorting
Before launch, manifests are topologically sorted using Kahn's
algorithm so that providers start before their dependents.
.Dq ORACLED
is an implicit provider that is always satisfied.
.Pp
Duplicate labels or
.Va provides
names across manifests are fatal.
A dependency cycle is a fatal error; no services are started.
Unknown providers are warned about but treated as satisfied.
.Ss Fork, Exec, and Coalitions
Each service is launched with
.Xr pdfork 2 ,
yielding a process descriptor that
.Nm
monitors via
.Dv EVFILT_PROCDESC
for
.Dv NOTE_EXEC
(exec confirmed) and
.Dv NOTE_EXIT
(process exited).
.Pp
Each service is enlisted in a coalition.
The process descriptor is set as the coalition leader, providing
resource grouping for the service and any children it creates.
.Ss Service States
A service transitions through the following states:
.Bl -tag -width "STOPPING (3)" -compact
.It STOPPED (0)
Not running.
.It STARTING (1)
Process created via
.Xr pdfork 2 ,
awaiting
.Dv NOTE_EXEC .
.It RUNNING (2)
.Dv NOTE_EXEC
received; service is executing.
.It STOPPING (3)
Graceful shutdown in progress.
.El
.Ss Restart Policies
.Bl -tag -width "on-failure"
.It Dq never
The service is not restarted.
.It Dq always
The service is restarted unconditionally after exit.
.It Dq on-failure
The service is restarted only if it exited with a non-zero status
or was killed by a signal.
.El
.Ss Linear Backoff
If a service dies within 5 seconds of starting (a rapid restart),
the restart is delayed with linear backoff: the delay is
.Va restart_count
multiplied by 2 seconds (i.e., 2, 4, 6, 8, ...), capped at
30 seconds.
If the service runs for at least 60 seconds, the restart counter
is reset.
.Ss Circuit Breaker
After
.Va max_failures
consecutive rapid failures (default 10), the service is permanently
disabled and not restarted.
A manifest reload via
.Dv SIGHUP
or the
.Cm reload
control socket command will re-evaluate the manifest.
.Ss Dynamic Claims
When
.Nm
launches a service, it mints capability tokens via the oracle pair
channel.
If the requested resource is not already claimed by the oracle,
the oracle auto-claims it dynamically with a global reference count.
.Pp
When a service exits,
.Nm
releases all capabilities from the service's manifest via the pair
channel.
Release messages are sent for every path, network endpoint, jail,
and system gate in the manifest.
The oracle decrements refcounts for dynamic claims; claims whose
refcount reaches zero are released from the kernel.
Policy claims
.Pq from Xr oracled.conf 5
return
.Er EPERM
on release, which is silently ignored.
.Pp
If
.Nm
itself exits or crashes, the oracle sweeps all dynamic claims,
releasing them from the kernel.
Policy claims survive across
.Nm
restarts.
.Pp
Releases use a batched send-then-drain pattern: all release messages
are sent in a burst, then replies are drained in a single blocking
window, regardless of how many capabilities are being released.
.Ss Graceful Shutdown
When stopping a service,
.Nm
sends
.Dv SIGTERM
via
.Xr pdkill 2
and starts a timer for the service's
.Va stop_timeout
(default 5 seconds).
If the service has not exited when the timer fires,
.Dv SIGKILL
is sent.
.Pp
During daemon shutdown, services are stopped in reverse dependency
order.
The kevent loop is drained for up to 60 seconds, after which
.Nm
closes the control socket and exits.
.Sh NAMING REGISTRY
.Nm
provides a naming registry that allows services to discover
and connect to each other using reverse-domain names
(e.g.,
.Dq org.freebsd.sshd ) .
.Pp
The registry is implemented as a hash table with 64 buckets.
Names may be up to 255 characters long.
Each service may register up to 32 names.
.Pp
Services interact with the registry via
.Xr libservice 3
over their pair channel to
.Nm .
The following operations are supported:
.Bl -tag -width "UNREGISTER"
.It Dv REGISTER
Register a reverse-domain name.
The name must contain at least one dot and consist only of
alphanumerics, dots, hyphens, and underscores.
The name must appear in the service's
.Va label
or
.Va provides
array; registration is denied otherwise.
Duplicate names are rejected with
.Er EEXIST .
.It Dv UNREGISTER
Remove a previously registered name.
Only the owning service may unregister a name.
.It Dv LOOKUP
Connect to a named service.
.Nm
creates a new cap_rt pair, pushes one end to the provider service
as a
.Dv SVC_OP_NEW_CLIENT
notification (which includes the requesting client's label),
and returns the other end to the requester.
A service cannot look up itself
.Pq Er ELOOP .
.El
.Pp
When a service exits, all names it registered are automatically
removed.
.Sh CONTROL SOCKET
.Nm
listens on a
.Ux Ns -domain
stream socket at
.Pa /var/run/serviced.sock
(mode 0700).
A maximum of 16 simultaneous connections are accepted, each with
a 2-second timeout.
.Pp
The
.Xr servicectl 8
utility communicates with
.Nm
over this socket.
.Pp
The following commands are supported:
.Bl -tag -width "SCTL_OP_LOAD (5)"
.It Dv SCTL_OP_STATUS (1)
Return daemon status and a summary of all loaded services with
their current state, PID, restart policy, and restart count.
Available to any user.
.It Dv SCTL_OP_SERVICES (2)
List all loaded services.
Same output as
.Dv SCTL_OP_STATUS .
Available to any user.
.It Dv SCTL_OP_RELOAD (3)
Reload manifests from disk.
New services are started, changed manifests trigger a graceful
restart, and removed manifests trigger a graceful stop.
The dependency graph is re-validated before any mutations are
applied; if the new graph contains a cycle, the reload is
rejected and running services are unaffected.
Requires root.
.It Dv SCTL_OP_CHECK (4)
Dry-run validation of a manifest file.
The payload is the filename to check.
Returns success if the manifest parses and validates correctly
without loading it.
Requires root.
.It Dv SCTL_OP_LOAD (5)
Load and start a single manifest file.
The payload is the filename to load.
The manifest is parsed, validated, and the service is started
immediately.
Requires root.
.El
.Sh SIGNALS
.Bl -tag -width "SIGTERM"
.It Dv SIGHUP
Reload service manifests.
Equivalent to
.Dv SCTL_OP_RELOAD .
.It Dv SIGTERM , SIGINT
Initiate graceful shutdown.
All services are stopped in reverse dependency order.
.Nm
exits after all services have terminated or been killed.
.It Dv SIGCHLD
Reap stray child processes.
.El
.Sh DTRACE PROBES
.Nm
provides DTrace USDT probes under the
.Ql serviced
provider.
.Ss Service Lifecycle
.Bl -tag -width "svc-disabled(label, count)" -compact
.It svc-start Ns ( Ns Ar label , pid Ns )
Service process created.
.It svc-exec Ns ( Ns Ar label , pid Ns )
Service exec confirmed via
.Dv NOTE_EXEC .
.It svc-exit Ns ( Ns Ar label , pid , status Ns )
Service process exited.
.It svc-restart Ns ( Ns Ar label , count Ns )
Service restart initiated.
.It svc-stop Ns ( Ns Ar label , pid Ns )
Service stop requested.
.It svc-load Ns ( Ns Ar label Ns )
Service manifest loaded.
.It svc-disabled Ns ( Ns Ar label , count Ns )
Service disabled by circuit breaker.
.It svc-count Ns ( Ns Ar n Ns )
Total loaded service count changed.
.El
.Ss Manifest Reload
.Bl -tag -width "svc-removed(label)" -compact
.It reload Ns ( Ns Ar nnew , nchanged , nremoved Ns )
Manifest reload completed.
.It svc-removed Ns ( Ns Ar label Ns )
Service removed during reload.
.It svc-changed Ns ( Ns Ar label Ns )
Service manifest changed during reload.
.El
.Ss Naming
.Bl -tag -width "naming-unregister(name)" -compact
.It naming-register Ns ( Ns Ar name , owner Ns )
Name registered.
.It naming-unregister Ns ( Ns Ar name Ns )
Name unregistered.
.It naming-lookup Ns ( Ns Ar name , requester Ns )
Name lookup performed.
.It naming-deny Ns ( Ns Ar name , errno Ns )
Name operation denied.
.It naming-count Ns ( Ns Ar n Ns )
Total registered name count changed.
.El
.Ss Control Socket
.Bl -tag -width "sctl-cmd-done(op, uid, status, duration_ns)" -compact
.It sctl-cmd Ns ( Ns Ar op , uid Ns )
Control command received.
.It sctl-cmd-done Ns ( Ns Ar op , uid , status , duration_ns Ns )
Control command completed.
.It sctl-deny Ns ( Ns Ar op , uid Ns )
Control command denied (insufficient privileges).
.El
.Ss Capabilities
.Bl -tag -width "cap-coalition(label, result)" -compact
.It cap-mint Ns ( Ns Ar label , type , result Ns )
Capability token minted.
.It cap-pair Ns ( Ns Ar label , result Ns )
Pair channel created.
.It cap-coalition Ns ( Ns Ar label , result Ns )
Coalition created.
.El
.Ss Exec Setup
.Bl -tag -width "svc-exec-done(label, duration_ns, ntokens)" -compact
.It svc-exec-done Ns ( Ns Ar label , duration_ns , ntokens Ns )
Service exec setup completed.
.It svc-exec-fail Ns ( Ns Ar label , errno Ns )
Service exec setup failed.
.El
.Ss IPC
.Bl -tag -width "ipc-reply(label, op, status)" -compact
.It ipc-recv Ns ( Ns Ar label , op Ns )
IPC message received from service.
.It ipc-reply Ns ( Ns Ar label , op , status Ns )
IPC reply sent to service.
.El
.Ss Timeouts
.Bl -tag -width "timeout-fire(label, type)" -compact
.It timeout-arm Ns ( Ns Ar label , type , seconds Ns )
Timer armed.
.It timeout-fire Ns ( Ns Ar label , type Ns )
Timer expired.
.El
.Ss Connections
.Bl -tag -width "conn-close(nconns)" -compact
.It conn-accept Ns ( Ns Ar uid , nconns Ns )
Control socket connection accepted.
.It conn-close Ns ( Ns Ar nconns Ns )
Control socket connection closed.
.El
.Ss Shutdown
.Bl -tag -width "shutdown-done(duration_ns)" -compact
.It shutdown-start Ns ( Ns Ar nservices Ns )
Graceful shutdown initiated.
.It shutdown-done Ns ( Ns Ar duration_ns Ns )
Shutdown completed.
.El
.Ss Errors
.Bl -tag -width "oracle-disconnected()" -compact
.It error Ns ( Ns Ar subsys , msg Ns )
Error occurred in subsystem.
.It oracle-disconnected Ns ( Ns )
Oracle pair channel closed unexpectedly.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/var/run/serviced.sock"
.It Pa /etc/serviced.d/
Default manifest directory.
Each
.Pa *.ucl
file declares a service.
.It Pa /var/run/serviced.sock
Control socket (mode 0700).
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Pp
.Nm
exits with an error if the
.Ev ORACLED_PAIR_FD
environment variable is not set or the pair fd is invalid.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Minimal service manifest:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# /etc/serviced.d/myservice.ucl
label = "myservice";
program = "/usr/local/sbin/myservice";
restart = "always";
.Ed
.Pp
Service with dependencies and capabilities:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
label = "webapp";
program = "/usr/local/sbin/webapp";
user = "www";
group = "www";
provides = ["http"];
requires = ["database"];
restart = "on-failure";
stop_timeout = 10;
max_failures = 20;
capabilities {
    paths = ["/var/www"];
    files = [
        {
            path = "/var/log/webapp.log";
            actions = ["write", "create", "append"];
        },
    ];
    network = [
        {
            port = 8080;
            protocol = "tcp";
            direction = "bind";
            address = "127.0.0.1";
        },
    ];
    system = ["sysctl"];
}
.Ed
.Pp
Service running inside a jail:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
label = "sandboxed";
program = "/usr/local/sbin/sandboxed";
restart = "on-failure";
jail {
    name = "sandboxed";
    path = "/var/jails/sandboxed";
    hostname = "sandboxed.local";
    ip4 = "10.0.0.2";
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kqueue 2 ,
.Xr pdfork 2 ,
.Xr libservice 3 ,
.Xr cap_rt 4 ,
.Xr oracled 8 ,
.Xr servicectl 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in 5BSD as the service manager for the Oracle
capability world.
